BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Water to Water: In conversation with Bonnie Devine & Bob Burl
 ey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T203000
UID:bm-6632520261103@shop.queenbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8100306/FWTW_cove
 r.png?cb=1792702383
DESCRIPTION:[In Store]\nIn 2020\, the McMichael invited Anishinaabe artist
  and scholar Bonnie Devine to help deepen the museum’s understanding of 
 the land it occupies and its place on the historic Toronto Carrying Place 
 Trail. During her research\, Devine encountered evidence of a 500-year-old
  Wendat village just a few kilometres from the museum. Conversations and r
 elationships with the Wendat Nation\, combined with her own artistic inqui
 ry\, ultimately led to the creation of From Water to Water: A Way Through 
 the Trees\, a mural installed at the McMichael in 2020. Conceived as a tem
 porary installation\, it remains a defining feature of the museum six year
 s later. Yet the questions that emerged from that work continued to expand
 . A new publication\, exhibition\, and artistic collaboration with settler
  photographer Robert Burley represent the next chapter of that journey.\nJ
 oin us for a panel discussion with the authors moderated by Sarah Milroy.
LOCATION:914 Queen Street East
URL:https://shop.queenbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Queen Books
END:VEVENT
